#limitation(title: [Stimulant Use in ME/CFS])[
Stimulants and wakefulness-promoting agents improve cognitive _symptoms_ but do not address the underlying pathology. The subjective improvement is plausibly mediated by arousal and reward-effort salience rather than by restored attention capacity: large-sample human evidence localizes stimulant action to arousal and reward networks, not attention-control networks @Kay2025stimulantarousalreward, and stimulants raise the willingness to invest effort without improving ability @Bowman2023NotSoSmart. They may enable patients to exceed their cognitive energy envelope, risking PEM. Clinicians should counsel patients that improved cognition from medication is not a signal to increase cognitive workload. For comprehensive pharmacological analysis of stimulant mechanisms, energy depletion risks, PEM dynamics, and harm reduction strategies, see Section @sec:stimulants.
]
